// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/analog/mos_psp103_data.t27 -- the IHP SG13G2 PSP103 current tables, per corner, from ngspice: data and nothing else
; M3b of the analog emulation epic (#10486, issue #10516); M3c (#10777, sub-issue #10880) adds the charge tables, THE CHARGE TABLES below, for tt and ss; M3c-3 (#10882) adds them for ff, fs and sf. M3a (specs/analog/mos_table.t27) reads a 25 x 25 table by exact-integer
; bilinear interpolation; this file holds the tables it reads when the device is the foundry's, Id(Vgs, Vds) of sg13_lv_nmos
; (W 1.0 um, L 0.45 um) and sg13_lv_pmos (W 3.0 um, L 0.45 um) for the five corners mos_tt, mos_ff, mos_ss, mos_fs and mos_sf, and the
; numbers the tests judge them by (held-out currents, the inverter's DC transfer, the inverter's transient). The functions are in
; mos_table.t27, the checks in mos_psp103.t27. Everything hand-written is the wrapper around the numbers, the pins and the accessors.
; -
; WHERE THE NUMBERS COME FROM. ngspice-47 and the IHP-Open-PDK checkout at commit 21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40: the model
; file ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib (PSP 103.6, revision 200310) with the model code
; ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/psp103/psp103.va of the same commit, compiled by OpenVAF-Reloaded v24.0.2mob to psp103.osdi. Temperature
; 27 C (TNOM 27 C). The decks are plain netlists with a .control block that prints the numbers, in specs/analog/decks/:
;   psp103_tab_tt.cir, _ff, _ss, _fs, _sf   the two tables, the inverter's DC transfer, the held-out currents (the tt deck also prints the
;                                         576 cell midpoints and 1000 R2 points; the others 200 R2 points)
;   psp103_inv_be.cir, psp103_inv_fine.cir   the inverter transient at 10 pF, backward Euler on a fixed 2 ns grid and a converged run
;   psp103_inv_be_500f.cir, psp103_inv_fine_500f.cir   the same at 500 fF and 100 ps: two crossing times each (the backward Euler deck
;                                         also prints the 401-sample waveform, INV500_BE)
;   psp103_q_tt.cir, psp103_q_ss.cir   (M3c) the drain and gate charge tables, the current tables again, and the capacitances ngspice reports at one point
;   psp103_q_ff.cir, psp103_q_fs.cir, psp103_q_sf.cir   (M3c-3) the same deck for the other three corners (only the title and the .lib section differ)
;   psp103_gate_node.cir   (M3c-3) a circuit with a gate node, the first that reads the gate charge: a PMOS drain, a bias resistor, a 25 fF
;                                         capacitor and an NMOS gate on one node, the node's waveform of ngspice backward Euler on a 5 ps grid (GATE_BE)
;   psp103_inv_be_500f_ss.cir, _ff, _fs, _sf   (M3c-3) psp103_inv_be_500f.cir (tt) for the other four corners: the 500 fF waveform of
;                                         ngspice backward Euler in that corner, the reference the charge tables of the corner are judged by
;   psp103_idpa_tt.cir   (M3c-2, #10881) the log-domain current tables of the tt corner, TT_LG_N and TT_LG_P, and 1000 held-out currents at cell centres of their grid
; Each is run as `IHP_PDK=<checkout> IHP_OSDI=<dir with psp103.osdi> ngspice -b <deck>`; no deck holds a path. ngspice rounds each current
; to a table unit itself (nint in the deck) and prints it between "BEGIN name" and "END name"; the rows were wrapped onto lines
; below in print order, none changed or reordered. The pins (order-sensitive folds, as M3a pins its run) fail on any changed number.
; -
; THE GRID AND THE UNITS. Id is tabulated on 25 x 25 nodes, 24 cells of 62.5 mV on each axis over 0 .. 1.5 V (the supply), index
; ix * 25 + iy with ix along Vgs and iy along Vds. This is the grid of M3a's reader: 24 cells of 2^20 units, so a unit is 2^-24 V
; (59.6 nV) and Vdd = 25165824. A table entry is Id * (dt / C) in volts per step, in units: dt / C = 200 V/A (2 ns on 10 pF, or 100 ps
; on 500 fF), so an entry is Id * 200 * 2^24 rounded and one unit is 0.298 nA. For the PMOS the axes are Vsg and Vsd, the source and
; bulk on the 1.5 V rail, and the entry is the current that leaves the drain. The largest entries (1.5 V, 1.5 V) are 402.3 uA (NMOS,
; 1349912) and 301.5 uA (PMOS, 1011527) at tt, below the 2^23 the solver's u64 interpolation allows. Negative entries (the gate current
; that leaves through the drain at Vds = 0 and Vgs above 1.2 V, at most 2 units = 0.6 nA) are held at 0: the table is unsigned.
; -
; THE HELD-OUT POINTS are never nodes of the grid. The tt deck prints the current in pA (nint(Id * 1e12)) at the 576 cell midpoints
; Vgs, Vds = (i + 1/2) * 62.5 mV, where a chord is worst, and at 1000 points of the R2 low-discrepancy sequence: point k = 1..1000 is
; Vgs (Vsg) = 1.5 frac(k * 0.7548776662466927) and Vds (Vsd) = 1.5 frac(k * 0.5698402909980532), 1/plastic number and its square; the
; other corners print the first 200 of those points. Each pair of devices has its own set of currents, the same coordinates.
; -
; THE CHARGE TABLES (M3c, issue #10777; M3c-3, issue #10882). Five more decks, specs/analog/decks/psp103_q_tt.cir, _ss, _ff, _fs and _sf (corners
; mos_tt, mos_ss, mos_ff, mos_fs, mos_sf; the five differ in the title and the .lib section only), print the DRAIN and GATE charge of each
; device on the same 25 x 25 grid: TT_QD_N TT_QG_N TT_QD_P TT_QG_P and the SS_, FF_, FS_, SF_ four.
; PSP103 reports no terminal charge as an output variable (`show` lists currents, conductances and the capacitances cdd, cdg, cgg, ...
; with the overlap cgdol and junction cjd apart), so the deck takes the whole charge of a terminal, channel plus overlap plus fringe plus
; junction, from the terminal CURRENT of one backward Euler step, which is the quantity ngspice integrates: Q(B) - Q(A) = (i_A - i_return) dt
; for a step to the grid node B and back to the origin A = (Vgs, Vds) = (0, 0), dt = 10 ns, where the device is off. The same deck run
; prints the current tables (grid_n, grid_p), which are byte for byte the corner's N and P tables (TT_N, TT_P, SS_N, SS_P, ...): the current
; tables and the charge tables come from one run of one netlist. A charge entry is Q / 500 fF in units of 2^-24 V (the voltage a 500 fF node moves when it takes the
; charge; one unit is 2.98e-20 C), relative to the origin plus 2^21 so that no entry is negative (only differences are physical); the PMOS
; tables are NEGATED, so that every drain table grows with Vds and every gate table with Vgs, as capacitances are positive. The scale
; ties a charge table to C = 500 fF, as a current table is tied to dt / C: for another load the entries scale by 500 fF / C.
; The tt and ss charge tables differ by 4.3 .. 5.3 % of their range (tt and ff by 4.7 .. 5.7 %, tt and fs or sf by 2.2 .. 2.8 %, fs and sf
; by 4.6 .. 5.3 %), which is why the negative control in mos_psp103.t27 is the delay and the waveform and not a count of volts. The 500 fF
; inverter of each of ss, ff, fs and sf is judged by its own ngspice backward Euler waveform (the four psp103_inv_be_500f_ss / _ff / _fs / _sf
; decks: SS_INV500_BE, FF_INV500_BE, FS_INV500_BE, SF_INV500_BE, with the two 0.75 V crossing times of each in fs), as the tt one is by INV500_BE.
; -
; THE GATE NODE (M3c-3). GATE_BE is the 401-sample waveform of one internal node g of a circuit in which g is the gate of an NMOS (drain at the rail, so
; the gate-charge table is read along Vds = 1.5 V) and is loaded by the drain of a PMOS whose gate steps (deck psp103_gate_node.cir; the gate edge is a
; jump of charge off the node, 0.15 V in the first step, before the PMOS current can act), by a 25 fF capacitor and by a 10 kohm bias resistor. dt =
; 5 ps on 25 fF is dt / C = 200 V/A again, so the current tables are the same words and the charge tables (Q / 500 fF) are scaled by 500 fF / 25 fF = 20.
; The node stays between 0.59 and 1.08 V, inside the tables' range.
; -
; THE LOG-DOMAIN CURRENT TABLES (M3c-2, issue #10881; tt only). TT_LG_N and TT_LG_P are a different table of the same two devices (sg13_lv_nmos W 1.0 um, sg13_lv_pmos
; W 3.0 um, L 0.45 um, IHP-Open-PDK 21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40, mos_tt, 27 C), made to be read in the log domain by the integer exp of mos_table.t27: the linear
; tables above cannot give 1 % in weak inversion (a word is 298 pA and a chord over a 62.5 mV cell is 41 % above an exponential at the middle; the tests of mos_psp103.t27).
; A node is not Id but Id / F, as log2 in 1/65536 of an octave (16 fraction bits, an integer part under 2^5, so a word is under 2^21 and the reader's u64 interpolation
; holds), measured in IUNIT = 2^-8 of a linear-table word = 1 / (200 * 2^32) A = 1.164 pA. F is the Vds factor of weak inversion, F = 1 - exp(-Vds / s(Vgs)), handled apart by the
; reader; s is the scale of a gate voltage, s(Vgs) = sqrt(0.030^2 + (0.65 * max(Vgs - 0.23, 0))^2) volts, 30 mV (a little over kT/q) in weak inversion where F is exactly the
; diffusion factor, growing to 0.6 V and more in strong inversion where the channel is a resistor and F is nearly linear: it is the one number per gate node that makes
; Id / F nearly flat along Vds in both regimes (without it the first Vds cells are 5 % chords). The reader multiplies Vds by rv = nint(4096 / s), 97 words, the last 97 of each
; table; a table is [tag word 4294967295, 4753 words, 97 words] in one slice, so the one name `tn` of the Newton step carries it. The grid is 97 x 49 nodes, Vgs = ix * 15.625 mV
; (96 cells of 2^18 voltage units) and Vds = iy * 31.25 mV (48 cells of 2^19), 1.5 V on each axis, index ix * 49 + iy, the grid of the 25 x 25 tables refined 4 x along Vgs and
; 2 x along Vds (the curvature of ln Id along Vgs near threshold is what sets 15.6 mV: 31.2 mV gives 1.5 %, 15.6 mV 0.5 %). The column Vds = 0 holds the limit of Id / F there,
; s_eff * gds0, with gds0 the output conductance ngspice reports at Vds = 0 (the one number printed from the model, not from a current); every other node is nint of the formula
; from ngspice's Id at that node. Id below 1 IUNIT (1.164 pA) is held at 1 IUNIT; the PMOS is read at Vsg and Vsd. The 576 midpoints of the 62.5 mV cells, the held-out set of the
; linear tables, are NODES of this grid (a read there tests the rounding and nothing else), and the 1000 R2 points are off the nodes but not at the worst place of this grid, so
; TT_CEN_N and TT_CEN_P add 1000 currents in pA at CENTRES of its cells (R2 picks the cell), where a chord of THIS grid is worst. The pins fail on any changed number.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. The numbers in this file are the numbers the decks printed, in order (the pins), the five corners are in the order
; the foundry names them (ff above tt above ss in drive current for both devices; fs a fast NMOS with a slow PMOS, sf the reverse), and
; the units are the ones the header states.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. That these are the tables a board loads: the board gets the same words, but no bitstream, BRAM or UART line is
; in this milestone. That the numbers are right: they are ngspice's, at its solver tolerances (reltol 1e-6, vntol 1e-9, abstol 1e-14),
; for the two device sizes and 27 C, nothing about another W, L, m, temperature, the high-voltage devices, mismatch or Monte Carlo.
; That PSP103 is a physical transistor: it is the foundry's model of one. The drain and gate charge is tabulated for all five corners
; (each with the 500 fF reference waveform of ngspice backward Euler of its corner), the source and bulk charge not at all (a source or
; bulk off the rail is not a circuit this file serves), and a charge table is for C = 500 fF.
; ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module AnalogMosPsp103Data;

use analog::linear::{fold};

; --- what the numbers are -------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const KIND : str = "analog-table-data";
pub const ID : str = "analog/mos_psp103_data";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "IHP-Open-PDK ihp-sg13g2 cornerMOSlv.lib (PSP 103.6) through ngspice-47 and OSDI";
